MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "Partners feels like a natural next choice because vocal duets connect with the polished crossover singing I enjoyed in A Musical Affair, Stages, and Lead With Your Heart.",
    "To Be Loved suits my interest in warm, expressive singing and traditional arrangements. The country selections and Christmas harmonies also connect with parts of my listening history, even though they are less appealing today."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "In The Lonely Hour, 25, and Oscd Ad Adele 21 emphasize contemporary pop vocals, while I currently want the orchestral support, ensemble singing, or traditional arrangements that make a vocal performance feel right to me.",
    "1989 does not offer the relaxing orchestral feel I want today. Django and Jimmie also stretches my interest in Golden and 747 further into traditional country than I would choose now."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "Enjoying expressive singers seems to have been treated as a broad interest in contemporary pop vocal albums, overlooking how much the accompaniment and style of singing matter to me.",
    "My past country and Christmas listening seems to carry too much weight as an immediate preference; those are occasional interests rather than what I seek on every visit."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My latest interaction with relaxing classical music suggests that calm arrangements and orchestral textures deserve more attention in what I might choose now.",
    "The repeated connection across my crossover and musical-theater listening is polished vocal performance with rich arrangements, which makes Partners and To Be Loved more compelling than a generally similar vocal album."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognize my interest in melodic singing but miss how strongly my choices today depend on polished crossover vocals, traditional arrangements, and a relaxing mood."
}
